  "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}{e}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{2y}dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{{y}^{2}}[\\,x\\,]_{0}^{2y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{{y}^{2}}(2y-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2y{e}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2y{e}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dy & ={[{e}^{{y}^{2}}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & ={e}^{1}-{e}^{0} \\\\  & =e-1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
